{
  "name": "Email a weekly social media performance digest and draft next week's posts with SocialRobot MCP and OpenAI",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Weekly social media digest with next week's drafts\n\nEvery Monday, get a short report on how last week's posts performed and a set of fresh drafts based on what worked, waiting in your SocialRobot calendar.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every Monday at 8am the workflow sets last week's date range.\n2. An AI agent connects to SocialRobot's MCP server with read-only analytics tools and pulls post metrics for each connected account.\n3. It writes a digest with headline numbers, top posts and recommendations, using only numbers SocialRobot returned.\n4. The digest is emailed to you as HTML.\n5. New post ideas are routed by network and saved as drafts in SocialRobot.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Create an API key at socialrobot.io/scheduler/api-keys and add it to **SocialRobot MCP** as a Bearer Auth credential\n- [ ] Install the SocialRobot community node with the same key, and pick an account in each **Draft on** node\n- [ ] Add OpenAI and Gmail credentials and your email in **Email the Digest**\n- [ ] Set language and brand voice in **Set Digest Options**\n\n### Customization\n- Analytics cover Instagram, Facebook, Threads, LinkedIn, Pinterest and TikTok. X, Bluesky and Mastodon receive drafts but are not analyzed.\n- Connect the optional Slack or X node (X needs SocialRobot Pro).\n- Change the range in **Set Digest Options**.",
        "width": 480,
        "height": 960
      },
      "id": "d3aa24be-e8ec-402f-b2a8-afa25414ea04",
      "name": "Template Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Collect last week's results\nSets the date range. The agent reads analytics through SocialRobot's MCP server and writes the digest and new post ideas.",
